          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em string orientation of tmf
            is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            for
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi M
                  %mi String
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma \;\colon\; M String \longrightarrow tmf
          %p
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+structure"} String structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (see there for more)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mi String
                      %mo ,
                      %mi rat
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi MF
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \;\colon\; \Omega^{String,rat}_\bullet \longrightarrow MF_\bullet
          %p
            (with values in the ring of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \simeq \pi_\bullet(\sigma)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For this reason the string orientation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            is also referred to as the “topological Witten genus”.
          %p
            All this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsStrickland01"}> Ando-Hopkins-Strickland 01
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"} Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10
          %p
            See the Idea-section at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            and at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            for more background.
          %h2#construction_via_cubical_structure Construction via Cubical structure
          %p
            The construction proceeds via the relation between orientations in complex orientable cohomology theory and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+structures+on+line+bundles"} cubical structures on line bundles
