          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The construction/identification of the string orientation and its relation to the Witten genus is due to
          %ul
            %li#AndoHopkinsStrickland01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic spectra, the Witten genus and the theorem of the cube
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s002220100175"} doi:10.1007/s002220100175
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/musix.pdf"} pdf
            %li#AndoHopkinsStrickland02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The sigma orientation is an H-infinity map
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0204053"} arXiv:math/0204053
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1353/ajm.2004.0008"} doi:10.1353/ajm.2004.0008
            %li#AndoHopkinsRezk10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Multiplicative orientations of
                    = succeed "-theory" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi KO
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://rezk.web.illinois.edu/koandtmf.pdf"} pdf
          %p following announcements of results in
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              ,
              %em Algebraic topology and modular forms
              in Proceedings of the International Congress of Mathematicians,
              %p
                Vol. I (Beijing, 2002), pages 291–317, Beijing, 2002. Higher Ed. Press (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212397"}> arXiv:math/0212397
                )
          %p which in turn follows the general program outlined in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological modular forms, the Witten genus, and the theorem of the cube
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathunion.org/ICM/ICM1994.1/Main/icm1994.1.0554.0565.ocr.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An alternative construction using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            is sketched in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 5.3 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
          %p
            In fact the construction there is a refinement of the orientation of just
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            to one of all
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            carrying a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curve"} derived elliptic curve
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Spec(A)
          %p
            Discussion in relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twists
            of
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
          %ul
            %li#ABG10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twists of K-theory and TMF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=PSPUM-81"} vol 81
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3004"} arXiv:1002.3004
          %p
            with some related chat in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Quantization+via+Linear+homotopy+types"} Quantization via Linear homotopy types
          %p
            Possible hints for further relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            are presented in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
              %em Holomorphic SCFTs with small index
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.00589"}> arXiv:1811.00589
              )
          %h3#ReferencesWithLevelStructure With level structure
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-orientation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi string
                      %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} string^h
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tmf%28n%29"} with level structure
          %ul
            %li#Devalapurkar
              Sanath K. Devalapurkar:
              %em
                A
                = succeed "-ANALOGUE" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi String
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Spin
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^{\mathbf{C}}
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://sanathdevalapurkar.github.io/files/string-analogue-spinc.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Devalapurkar-StringAnalogue.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and further developed with possible application to
            = succeed "-cancellation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DMW+anomaly"} DMW anomaly
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"}> Arun Debray
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Yu"} Matthew Yu
              %em Type IIA String Theory and tmf with Level Structure
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.07299"}> arXiv:2411.07299
              \&amp;rbrack;
